<section class="ch-s ch-lt"><div class="ch-w ch-gh"><div><p class="ch-ey"><i></i>The registers</p><h2 class="rv">Four ways to lay out a dial</h2></div><p class="ch-hint">Drag &rarr;</p></div><div class="hs ch-hs"><div class="ch-cx"><div class="ch-cx-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1564496954841-092e3a3bda16?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=660&q=75" alt="a black analog watch on a dark surface" width="520" height="660" loading="lazy"></div><span>01</span><h3>Two-register</h3><p>Minutes and running seconds, symmetrical and calm.</p></div><div class="ch-cx"><div class="ch-cx-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1610006329898-2a4f12019450?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=660&q=75" alt="a black chronograph watch with orange accents held in a hand" width="520" height="660" loading="lazy"></div><span>02</span><h3>Racing</h3><p>High-contrast hands and a tachymeter for the track.</p></div><div class="ch-cx"><div class="ch-cx-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1624124834665-eecde7bf50e7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=660&q=75" alt="a black and silver chronograph watch on a wrist" width="520" height="660" loading="lazy"></div><span>03</span><h3>Three-register</h3><p>Seconds, minutes and hours, the classic layout.</p></div><div class="ch-cx"><div class="ch-cx-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1589936360188-05a53d811713?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=660&q=75" alt="a silver chronograph watch with a black leather strap" width="520" height="660" loading="lazy"></div><span>04</span><h3>Dress chronograph</h3><p>Slim, quiet and made for a cuff.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="ch-s ch-ty" id="tachy"><div class="ch-w ch-ty-g"><div><p class="ch-ey"><i></i>Instrument No. 2</p><h2 class="rv">Speed, from seconds</h2><p class="ch-p">Time a known distance, one kilometre or one mile, and the tachymeter gives you speed. Move the slider to the seconds it took.</p><label class="ch-lab" for="ty-s">Seconds over the distance <output id="ty-sv">36 s</output><input type="range" id="ty-s" min="7" max="60" value="36"></label><div class="ch-unit" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Distance unit"><label><input type="radio" name="tu" value="km" checked><span>1 kilometre</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="tu" value="mi"><span>1 mile</span></label></div></div><div class="ch-ty-o"><svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="128" class="t-r"/><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="128" class="t-p" id="ty-arc" pathLength="60"/><line x1="150" y1="150" x2="150" y2="34" id="ty-h" class="t-h"/><circle cx="150" cy="150" r="5" fill="#E8622C"/></svg><div class="ch-ty-v"><b id="ty-o">100</b><span id="ty-u">km/h</span></div></div></div></section>

<section class="ch-qt"><div class="ch-qt-i pxw"><img data-px=".12" src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1723629159965-b0628625f45e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1800&h=900&q=75" alt="a watch face in close-up on a black surface" width="1800" height="900" loading="lazy"></div><blockquote class="ch-w"><p class="rv">&ldquo;The hand that leaps when you press the pusher is the whole point. Everything else is the watch.&rdquo;</p><cite>The Chronos editors</cite></blockquote></section>

